const DIAGNOSTIC={"intro":"Sixteen questions, about ten minutes. It recommends where to start; it locks nothing. Choose \"Not sure\" rather than guessing: a guess that happens to be right sends you past something you'd benefit from.","areas":["Power Query","Modeling","DAX","Service","Security","Performance","Deployment","Fabric"],"questions":[{"area":"Power Query","level":"beginner","topic":"b-pq","q":"A price column holds \"$1,299.00\", \"N/A\" and blanks. Which order of steps loads it as a number with no errors?","o":["Change the type to Decimal first, then remove errors","Replace \"$\" and \",\" with nothing and \"N/A\" with null, then change the type","Split the column by \"$\", then change the type","Filter out the rows that contain \"$\""],"a":1,"why":"Clean the text first, then convert. Converting first creates errors, and removing errors deletes real rows."},{"area":"Modeling","level":"beginner","topic":"b-model","q":"In a star schema, which statement is true?","o":["Fact tables filter dimension tables","Every table should relate to every other table","Dimension tables filter the fact table through one-to-many relationships","Bi-directional filtering is the recommended default"],"a":2,"why":"Filters flow from the one side (dimension) to the many side (fact). Bi-directional is the exception, not the default."},{"area":"DAX","level":"beginner","topic":"b-dax","q":"Why is Total Sales usually a measure rather than a calculated column?","o":["Calculated columns can't be formatted as currency","A measure is evaluated in the current filter context when the visual asks, and doesn't store a value on every row","Measures are computed at refresh, so they are faster","Only measures can be used in slicers"],"a":1,"why":"Measures respond to filters at query time. Calculated columns are computed at refresh and stored per row, which costs memory and doesn't react to slicers."},{"area":"Service","level":"beginner","topic":"b-service","q":"You fix a report and publish it to the workspace, but people using the app still see the old version. Why?","o":["Their browser cache needs clearing","App users only see changes after someone selects Update app","They need a Pro licence to see changes","The scheduled refresh failed"],"a":1,"why":"An app is a published snapshot of workspace content. Workspace changes reach app users when the app is updated."},{"area":"Power Query","level":"intermediate","topic":"i-pq","q":"Against SQL Server, which step is most likely to stop query folding?","o":["Filtering rows on a date column","Removing columns","Renaming a column","Adding a column that calls a custom M function on every row"],"a":3,"why":"Most built-in steps translate to SQL. A custom function invoked per row usually can't, so everything after it runs in the mashup engine."},{"area":"Modeling","level":"intermediate","topic":"i-model","q":"Budget is stored per Month and Product Category. Actuals are per day and product. How should Budget relate to the model?","o":["Relate Budget to DimProduct[ProductKey] directly","Relate it at its own grain: to a Category-level dimension (or with TREATAS) and to a month-level date attribute","Copy budget onto every sales row in Power Query","Use a many-to-many relationship on ProductName"],"a":1,"why":"A fact must join at its grain. Budget has no product or day, so it relates to the attributes it does have."},{"area":"DAX","level":"intermediate","topic":"i-dax","q":"In a matrix row for Color = Blue, what does CALCULATE([Sales], Product[Color] = \"Red\") return?","o":["Blank","Sales for Blue","Sales for Red, because the filter argument replaces the Color filter from the row","Sales for Red and Blue together"],"a":2,"why":"A boolean filter argument overwrites the existing filter on that column. KEEPFILTERS would intersect it instead and give blank."},{"area":"Service","level":"intermediate","topic":"i-service","q":"When does a scheduled refresh need an on-premises data gateway?","o":["Always","When the source is on-premises or in a private network the Power BI service can't reach","Only for Excel files","Never for SQL Server"],"a":1,"why":"Cloud sources reachable from the internet don't need one. On-premises or private-network sources do."},{"area":"Security","level":"intermediate","topic":"i-rls","q":"A report page filter hides other regions from regional managers. Is that security?","o":["Yes, if the report is shared through an app","No. Filters can be changed or bypassed (Build permission, Analyze in Excel). Use RLS roles","Yes, if the filter pane is hidden","Only for users without a Pro licence"],"a":1,"why":"A filter is a presentation choice. Row-level security is enforced by the engine for every query, whatever the tool."},{"area":"Performance","level":"advanced","topic":"a-perf","q":"Server Timings show 90% of the time in the formula engine and thousands of tiny storage engine queries. Most likely cause?","o":["Too many columns in the model","An iterator evaluating a measure row by row, causing many storage engine requests (or callbacks)","A slow network between the browser and the service","The gateway is overloaded"],"a":1,"why":"Thousands of small SE queries plus FE-heavy time is the signature of row-by-row evaluation. Rewrite so the storage engine aggregates in a few big queries."},{"area":"Performance","level":"advanced","topic":"a-perf","q":"Which column usually costs the most memory in an Import model?","o":["A Yes/No flag","A low-cardinality text column such as Region","A high-cardinality column such as a transaction ID or a datetime to the second","An integer foreign key with 50 values"],"a":2,"why":"VertiPaq compresses by dictionary. Millions of distinct values mean a huge dictionary and poor compression."},{"area":"Security","level":"advanced","topic":"a-gov","q":"Some users may see every row but must not see the Salary column at all. Use:","o":["Row-level security","Object-level security on the Salary column","Hide the column in the model","A perspective without Salary"],"a":1,"why":"Hidden columns and perspectives are conveniences, not security. OLS makes the column not exist for that role."},{"area":"Deployment","level":"advanced","topic":"a-deploy","q":"Why save a team's model as PBIP rather than PBIX?","o":["The file is smaller","The model and report are saved as text (TMDL and PBIR) that Git can diff, review and merge","Refresh is faster","Apps require PBIP"],"a":1,"why":"PBIX is a binary package. PBIP is a folder of documented text files, so changes can be reviewed and merged."},{"area":"Deployment","level":"advanced","topic":"a-deploy","q":"Test and Production must read different source servers without anyone editing the file. Use:","o":["Two copies of the PBIX","A parameter for the server plus a deployment rule (or variable) per stage","Edit the connection in Production after each deployment","Row-level security"],"a":1,"why":"Parameters plus per-stage rules keep one artefact and make the environment difference explicit and repeatable."},{"area":"Fabric","level":"advanced","topic":"a-fabric","q":"Which Direct Lake option never falls back to DirectQuery?","o":["Direct Lake on SQL analytics endpoint","Direct Lake on OneLake","Both, when fallback is disabled in the gateway","Neither: all Direct Lake models can fall back"],"a":1,"why":"Direct Lake on OneLake runs only in Direct Lake mode; conditions that would cause fallback make the query fail instead. Direct Lake on SQL can fall back."},{"area":"Fabric","level":"advanced","topic":"a-fabric","q":"What does framing (refreshing) a Direct Lake model do?","o":["Copies all the data into the model again","Points the model at the latest version of each Delta table, without copying data","Converts the model to Import mode","Sends a query to the SQL endpoint for every visual"],"a":1,"why":"Framing reads Delta metadata. Columns load into memory later, when queries need them."}]};
